Two kinds of entry, one trail
On the left, a sealed payload travelling: each hop that carries it leaves a
travel entry, which is about the task and answers where this went. On the
right, somebody opening it: that leaves an access entry on the document, which
answers who read this — or leaves no entry at all, which is the trail saying
nobody looked. Beneath, the one read deliberately not recorded: the
machinery's own read to seal the payload, which yields only ciphertext and is
therefore not a disclosure.
